    "repository": {
      "pullRequest": {
        "number": 32830,
        "title": "fix(clients): unloaded thread links show their title and project icon",
        "url": "https://github.com/pingdotgg/t3code/pull/32830",
        "state": "MERGED",
        "isDraft": false,
        "body": "Existing threads appeared as \"Thread no longer available\" when their metadata was absent from the client's loaded thread list. Searching for the thread made the link recover.\n\nResolve unloaded links with a small read of the title and project ID, then use the existing project icon renderer. Web, desktop, and mobile keep the destination clickable while the read is pending or offline. The read includes archived threads and excludes deleted threads. Loaded threads retain the existing fast path. No conversation history or thread families are loaded, and no new cache or state store is added.\n\nLegacy links check their source environment before guessing a match elsewhere. Literal IDs take precedence over percent-decoded fallbacks. Older servers retain the title-only fallback and generic icon until their server supports the metadata read.\n\nValidation: `vp run check:changed`, including browser navigation regressions for title/icon loading, pending and offline reads, legacy environment resolution, percent-encoded IDs, and missing targets. Server tests cover archived and deleted metadata; client runtime tests cover current and older servers.\n\nRelated: #26467, #32541. This overlaps #26472, #30709, and #30635, using a metadata-only read rather than loading thread families or leaving titles unresolved.\n\nImplemented with GPT-6.1-Sol through the Codex harness in T3 Code.\n",
        "createdAt": "2026-11-08T05:02:55Z",
